{"blocks": [{"block_index": 0, "checksum": "3019313160", "data": "# metadata: references metadata/ folder\n\"\"\"Vision module for handling Multimodal (image) capture and", "line_end": 5, "line_start": 0}, {"block_index": 1, "checksum": "3281377610", "data": "# Reed-Solomon(255,223), GF(2^8) Galois Chunk parity protection\n# [Citation: Reed, I.S. & Solomon, G", "line_end": 10, "line_start": 5}, {"block_index": 2, "checksum": "2806241837", "data": "# 1. Split parity enables 10% data recovery (RS 5% + GC 5%)\n# 2. RS parity uses Galois Field multipl", "line_end": 15, "line_start": 10}, {"block_index": 3, "checksum": "2056091842", "data": "# 1. THEOREM: Any 5% data loss can be recovered\n#    PROOF: Reed-Solomon(255,223) can correct up to ", "line_end": 20, "line_start": 15}, {"block_index": 4, "checksum": "1270387021", "data": "    try:\n      \"\"\"Generate split parity for a source file.\n\n      Creates RS and GC parity blocks wi", "line_end": 25, "line_start": 20}, {"block_index": 5, "checksum": "170512288", "data": "      GC: Galois Chunk parity blocks via weighted XOR (5% overhead)\n\n      -- AXIOMS --\n      1. Sou", "line_end": 30, "line_start": 25}, {"block_index": 6, "checksum": "2639958585", "data": "      3. GC parity is computed as weighted XOR of blocks\n      4. Checksums are computed for each pa", "line_end": 35, "line_start": 30}, {"block_index": 7, "checksum": "1844381568", "data": "        References: https://parchive.sourceforge.net/\n      - MacWilliams, F.J. & Sloane, N.J.A. (19", "line_end": 40, "line_start": 35}, {"block_index": 8, "checksum": "3845315783", "data": "          block_size: Size of each parity block in bytes (default: 512)\n\n      Returns:\n          di", "line_end": 45, "line_start": 40}, {"block_index": 9, "checksum": "1786570349", "data": "      # parity: atomic_encode_result applied (SECDED TED)\n      # invariants: function preconditions", "line_end": 50, "line_start": 45}, {"block_index": 10, "checksum": "1537840772", "dat